# Infinity SMP — All-in-One Discord Bot v2

A practical Discord.js 14 bot for Infinity SMP.

## Included
- Moderation: /ban /kick /timeout /untimeout /warn /warnings /clear /lock /unlock /slowmode
- Logs: /logs setup|status|channel|disable + member/message/mod/role/channel/voice/ticket/minecraft events
- AutoMod: /automod on|off|word|unword|status
- Tickets: /ticket setup|close with support/report/bug/partner buttons
- Applications: /application setup with staff/creator/partner/whitelist modals
- Welcome: /welcome channel|off
- Messages: /embed /announce /say /poll
- Utilities: /userinfo /serverinfo /avatar /servericon /ping /botinfo /role /giverole
- Economy: /balance /daily /work /pay /leaderboard /shop
- Games: /coinflip /dice /8ball /rps /guess
- Utility automation: /remind /giveaway
- Minecraft bridge: /mcstatus /link /unlink /mcplayer /mcchat plus HTTP endpoints
- Persistent JSON data in data/db.json

## Setup
1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.
2. Set DISCORD_TOKEN, CLIENT_ID, GUILD_ID and MC_BRIDGE_SECRET.
3. Run `npm install`.
4. Run `npm start`.

## Important
Keep the bot token private. The bot must have the permissions required by the commands you use.
Music playback, a web dashboard, and production SQL storage are intentionally not included in this v2 package; those require additional services/dependencies and should not be presented as implemented when they are not.


## Web Dashboard

The bot includes a Discord OAuth2 dashboard. Add these to `.env`: `DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET`, `DASHBOARD_PORT=3001`, and `DASHBOARD_REDIRECT_URI`. In Discord Developer Portal, add the redirect URL under OAuth2 redirects. Start the bot with `npm start`, then open `http://localhost:3001`. The dashboard provides Discord login, server selection, embed builder, announcements, channel/role creation, moderation, and bot settings. For a public website, deploy this project to a Node.js host and change the redirect URL to your HTTPS domain.


## V6 Pro Dashboard additions
- Professional ticket panel builder with dropdown topics, staff role, category, transcript channel, custom colors/text/banner, claim/close controls.
- Per-command dashboard controls: enable/disable, description override, category, allowed roles, denied roles, allowed channels, response visibility.
- Discord command sync endpoint for the selected guild.
- Dashboard remains OAuth-protected and can be owner-locked with `DASHBOARD_OWNER_ID`.

